<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Barbatos.SecsGem.MaterialFlow</PackageId>
    <TargetFrameworks>$(BarbatosTargetFrameworks)</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Barbatos.SecsGem.MaterialFlow</RootNamespace>
    <PackageTags>secs;e87;e90;e40;carrier;substrate;slotmap;processjob;wafer;fab300;materialflow</PackageTags>
    <Description>The joins between the material-flow standards for .NET, which none of them makes itself. E87 to E90: a carrier's verified slot map becomes one tracked substrate per occupied slot, forgotten again when the carrier is done - with the naming, the occupancy rule and the destination all replaceable. E40 to E90: a process job's ending reaches the wafers it was running, so a stopped job stops the work in progress and skips what nobody got to, instead of leaving a lot half tracked for ever. Depends on Barbatos.SecsGem.Carriers, Barbatos.SecsGem.Substrates and Barbatos.SecsGem.ProcessJobs, which stay independent of each other.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The only package in this repository that depends on several standards at once, which is
         the whole reason it exists: none of E87, E90 and E40 may depend on another, so the joins
         between them cannot live in any of them. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Carriers\Barbatos.SecsGem.Carriers.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.Substrates\Barbatos.SecsGem.Substrates.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Barbatos.SecsGem.ProcessJobs\Barbatos.SecsGem.ProcessJobs.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
